Set battery thresholds for the 4S 1550 mAh pack

The failsafe thresholds were still 3S values (10.5 V / 10.0 V), which a 4S
pack never reaches: the low-battery failsafe would simply never fire.

- BATTERY_LOW_V      10.5 -> 14.0  (3.50 V/cell -> land)
- BATTERY_CRITICAL_V 10.0 -> 13.2  (3.30 V/cell -> cut motors)
- BATTERY_CELLS         3 -> 4
- MAX_CURRENT_A      20.0 -> 2.0   the INA219 only sees the BEC branch
  (its 0.1 ohm shunt handles ~3.2 A), so 20 A could never trigger; 2 A
  now detects a short in the electronics. Stuck-motor protection relies on
  the voltage-sag and tilt-limit failsafes.

Docs updated for the 4S 1550 mAh pack. Firmware builds, 136/136 host tests
pass.

